// F89 (docs/UPSTREAM_FINDINGS.md): a lambda written with braces cannot appear in a mapping test's function.
// The mapping lexer reads `{` as a brace only after `:` or `[` (MappingLexerGrammar.g4's BRACE_OPEN); anywhere else
// it opens a class mapping's island, so `->filter({x|...})` in a suite's function does not parse. The same lambda
// parses in a service's query (Service demo::Braced). Run each file alone:
//   bazel run //tools/engine-runner:testable -- <this file> --testable=demo::M --testable=demo::Braced
// model.pure passes both (a suite without braces, a service with them); braced.pure is the same suite with braces,
// and the whole file fails to parse: "no viable alternative at input '->filter({x|$x.id == 'A1''".
Class demo::Acct
{
  id: String[1];
}

###Relational
Database demo::DB ( Table ACCT (ID VARCHAR(20) PRIMARY KEY) )

###Mapping
Mapping demo::M
(
  demo::Acct: Relational
  {
    ~primaryKey ([demo::DB]ACCT.ID)
    ~mainTable [demo::DB]ACCT
    id: [demo::DB]ACCT.ID
  }

  testSuites:
  [
    filtered:
    {
      function: |demo::Acct.all()->filter(x|$x.id == 'A1')->project(~[id:x|$x.id]);
      tests:
      [
        t:
        {
          data: [ demo::DB: Reference #{ demo::Seed }# ];
          asserts: [ a: EqualToJson #{ expected: ExternalFormat #{ contentType: 'application/json'; data: '[{"id":"A1"}]'; }#; }# ];
        }
      ];
    }
  ]
)

###Connection
RelationalDatabaseConnection demo::Conn
{ store: demo::DB; type: H2; specification: LocalH2 { }; auth: DefaultH2; }

###Runtime
Runtime demo::RT { mappings: [ demo::M ]; connections: [ demo::DB: [ environment: demo::Conn ] ]; }

###Data
Data demo::Seed
{ Relational #{ default.ACCT: 'ID\n' + 'A1\n' + 'A2\n'; }# }

###Service
Service demo::Braced
{
  pattern: '/braced';
  documentation: 'The braced lambda the suite cannot hold, in a service query, where it parses.';
  execution: Single
  {
    query: |demo::Acct.all()->filter({x|$x.id == 'A1'})->project(~[id:x|$x.id]);
    mapping: demo::M;
    runtime: demo::RT;
  }
  testSuites:
  [
    s:
    {
      data: [ connections: [ environment: Reference #{ demo::Seed }# ] ]
      tests:
      [
        t: { serializationFormat: PURE_TDSOBJECT; asserts: [ a: EqualToJson #{ expected: ExternalFormat #{ contentType: 'application/json'; data: '[{"id":"A1"}]'; }#; }# ] }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
